<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parliament of Åland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1922</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Lagting</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Parliament of Åland, the Lagting, is the legislature of the self-governing Åland Islands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>. It first met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mariehamn">Mariehamn</a> in 1922 under the autonomy settlement confirmed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-sundblom">Julius Sundblom</a> as its first speaker. Its 30 members, elected for four years, make laws on education, culture, policing, health and the local economy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/parliament-of-aland.jpg" alt="Parliament of Åland" width="320" height="165" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Henninng · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C3%85land_Lagting_2023.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
